[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3506629541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112523#issuecomment-3506629541","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112523","id":3506629541,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RAuul","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-08T15:20:13Z","updated_at":"2025-11-08T15:20:13Z","body":"My _quick 2 cents_ on this matter: I'm not sure this is really problematic. Unless there is some significant performance impact due to unnecessary new lines in the script file, this feels like an implementation detail that has no impact on the running project.\n\nAnd regarding \"multiline comments `\"\"\"`\", AFAIK these are plain strings, not really comments. So they could have more semantic value than comments, and therefore extending the behavior to stripping them inside functions could introduce issues.\n\nNot sure why comments are not stripped on shaders though; I don't see an argument not to do it in this case.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api